id: pm-c3uru0
title: "Sentry PM-CLI-2W: rejected unknown-author acknowledgments are emitted as high production errors"
description: "The public unknown-author acknowledgment command correctly rejects a stale or non-actionable target, but the handled TypeError crosses the observability boundary as a high unresolved Sentry issue. This makes expected operator validation noise indistinguishable from a product failure and can block release health."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:observability",author,sentry,ux
created_at: "2026-08-06T21:16:53.374Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T05:39:52.585Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-07T05:39:52.480Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-07T05:39:52.480Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: The observability boundary classifies this exact validation family as expected without masking unexpected errors; focused tests prove positive and negative classification; the Sentry release gate recognizes the outcome; PM-CLI-2W is dispositioned with live evidence.
goal: trustworthy-observability
objective: Keep release health sensitive to genuine failures without penalizing expected validation paths.
value: Preserves a trustworthy Sentry signal and avoids false release blockers.
impact: Reduces high-severity alert noise while retaining structured operator feedback.
outcome: The same invalid request remains rejected but no longer appears as an unresolved high production failure.
why_now: Live closeout found PM-CLI-2W as the only unresolved issue seen in the last 24 hours.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: medium
environment: production
repro_steps: "Run the unknown-author acknowledgment command against a stale or non-actionable event target such as pm-iimv:1; observe a handled CLI rejection and Sentry PM-CLI-2W."
resolution: "Replaced five bare TypeErrors in the acknowledgment primitive with one refusal helper raising PmCliError at the usage exit code with the codes selector_conflict, required_values_missing, target_unreadable and target_not_actionable; the CLI boundary already treats usage as expected, so the family is excluded at the source. Declared the four refusal families in the release gate expected-handled patterns and asserted the declaration in the release contract spec. Focused positive and negative classification tests added."
expected_result: "The exact invocation that produced the blocking production issue refuses without reaching the error channel, and unexpected failures inside the same primitive stay reportable"
actual_result: The same event coordinate exits 2 with a structured envelope carrying history_author_acknowledge_target_unreadable; the negative control proves a non-validation failure is still a non-PmCliError Error; full suite green at 6904 tests
affected_version: 2026.8.5
component: CLI observability boundary
regression: false
customer_impact: Release operators see a high unresolved production error for a correctly rejected request; no data corruption occurred.
